      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thanks for calling that out. 😅\n\nI did an instrumented run to figure out the actually correct factor, which resulted in ~7.6 file map entries per target on Chromium. I then re-ran the benchmarks on my c4d-384 VM again: 1) with the reserve using factor `3`, 2) completely without it, and 3) with an exact count computed from sources plus public headers.\n\nAs it turned out, this particular optimization did exactly... nothing.\n\nMedians of 10 round-robin rounds of `gn gen --check`: 3.98 s, 4.05 s, 4.00 s. That is within noise, so I just dropped the line.",
